353:As our first result, we prove that for all our testbed classes~${\cal H}$,  {\sc ${\cal H}$-Identification} is \NP-complete, except for the cases where ${\cal H}$ is  the class of paths or linear forests. Specifically, when ${\cal H}$ is the class of paths, the problem is known to be solvable in $O(n^3)$ time~\cite{Vikas13algo}. We show that the proof of this result can be extended to hold even for linear forests.
