new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9501ed8513076493039c10b44dbc9e3576c2d47c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@
+# arXiv 2604.24325 — exact linear-forest identification
+
+Status: the generator and all local gates pass, but the required four-vendor
+hardening verdict is **not yet available**. OpenRouter rejected every script-owned
+attempt with HTTP 403 (`Key limit exceeded (total limit)`). The error transcripts
+are retained; this result must not be submitted as hardened until those runs are
+repeated with a usable key.
+
+| Profile field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
+| Native domain | combinatorics |
+| Object regime | finite discrete |
+| Computational core | exact cover |
+| Certificate | integer tuple (an unordered partition into 4-path blocks) |
+| Native objects | linear forests represented by exact path-component lengths; endpoint-concatenation partition |
+| Intuition | invariant: four paths destined for one target share a residue modulo 997 |
+| Domain essentiality | native |
+| Reduction | none |
+
+## The problem and why the witness is trustworthy
+
+The source and target are linear forests—disjoint unions of paths—represented
+exactly by their component lengths. The solver partitions all source paths into
+blocks of four. Identifying three pairs of endpoints in a block concatenates its
+four paths, so a certificate is valid exactly when the block sums form the target
+length multiset. `verify` checks shape, IDs, exact coverage, integer sums, and that
+multiset; it never reads `inst["answer"]`.
+
+This is the paper's own object and witness language. Section 1 defines an
+identification and the equivalent witness partition. Observation 1, Proposition 1,
+and Theorem 2 use partitions of source components and concatenation of paths in
+exactly this way. See [Golovach, Morelle, and Paulusma, *Identification to
+Subclasses of Chordal Graphs*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.24325).
+
+Generation is inverse: distinct residues and four quotients are sampled first,
+the four source lengths are formed as `997*q+r`, and only then is their target
+length defined as their sum. Source and target orders are independently shuffled.
+No completed instance is searched to recover the planted partition.
+
+## Why Track B, not Track A
+
+The paper draws the easy boundary clearly. Corollary 1 makes identification to the
+*class* of linear forests polynomial. For an explicitly supplied target linear
+forest, Theorem 2 proves W[1]-hardness in the number of target components, while
+Lemma 6 gives an `O(nm + n^(t+1))` XP dynamic program. The theorem is worst-case;
+it does not prove this planted distribution hard. A Track-A claim would therefore
+be false or at least unsupported.
+
+The successful reference algorithm for this restricted family enumerates source
+pair sums, performs a complement lookup for every target/pair combination, and
+runs Algorithm X on the resulting exact-cover rows. At provisional shipping
+`n=256`, it solved 8/8 instances, averaging 4,243,905 counted operations and 2.13
+seconds. That is the honest mechanical route. After recognizing the invariant,
+the compact route performs exactly 256 reductions modulo 997 and groups equal
+residues. The benchmark tests finding that invariant without a tool; it does not
+claim computational intractability.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+The `demo` preset with seed 0 renders the following complete instance:
+
+```text
+Exact identification of one linear forest with another
+
+A path's length is its number of edges.  A linear forest is a disjoint union of
+paths.  The source forest G below has 8 path components; source ID i denotes a
+path of the displayed length.  The target forest L has 2 path components, whose
+displayed order is irrelevant.
+
+Identifying two vertices replaces them by one vertex adjacent to the union of
+their neighbors.  In particular, identifying an endpoint of one path with an
+endpoint of a disjoint path concatenates them into a path whose length is the sum
+of the two lengths.
+
+Find an endpoint-concatenation witness: partition all source IDs into exactly 2
+unordered blocks of exactly four distinct IDs. Every ID 1 through 8 occurs once,
+and the multiset of the two block sums must equal the target-length multiset.
+
+Source components, as ID:length:
+  1:10834  2:14822  3:12828  4:14352  5:10364  6:8840  7:15349  8:11361
+
+Target components, as ID:length:
+  1:51426  2:47324
+```
+
+The answer is `<answer>[[1,2,3,6],[4,5,7,8]]</answer>`.
+
+```python
+>>> verify(inst, [[1, 2, 3, 6], [4, 5, 7, 8]])
+(True, 'ok')
+>>> verify(inst, [[4, 2, 3, 6], [4, 5, 7, 8]])
+(False, 'a source component ID is repeated')
+```
+
+A person can solve this eight-item illustration by checking the 35 possible
+four/four partitions (or by spotting the modular structure); exact enumeration
+finds one valid certificate.
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| Preset | Source paths `n` | Target paths | Quotient bits | Answer atoms | Status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 8 | 2 | 4 | 8 | hand-scale, skipped by hardener |
+| easy | 192 | 48 | 24 | 192 | oracle calls blocked externally |
+| medium | 224 | 56 | 27 | 224 | not reached |
+| hard | 256 | 64 | 30 | 256 | provisional shipping preset |
+
+`SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY` remains `hard` pending a successful oracle run. If the
+hardener finds a lower rung holds, it must be changed to that rung and the gates
+rerun. Escalation stops with `cap_bound` after 256 paths because another complete
+partition would exceed the 256-atom output cap.
+
+## Local gate results
+
+| Gate | Result | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 20/20 planted witnesses; every preset × 5 seeds; JSON-native |
+| G2 | pass | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | fenced JSON inside realistic prose round-trips; garbage returns `None` |
+| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 valid uniform structure-aware partitions at hard |
+| G5 | pass | hard density 0/200,000; demo exact count 1/35; reference cost 4,243,905 operations mean |
+| G6 | pass | six attacks, each 0/8; reference exact cover 8/8 as expected |
+| G7 | pass | doubled `n=512` builds, verifies, and has a larger search space |
+| G8 | pass | 20 target reorderings, 20 carried source relabelings, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | pass | 1,045 characters, 262 estimated tokens, 256 atoms, 256 intended exact operations |
+
+The six failing attacks are magnitude chunks, input-order chunks, last-three-
+decimal-digit chunks, a global difference-GCD bucket guess, residual-average
+greedy packing, and 512 uniform restarts. The domain-standard pair-sum/Algorithm-X
+solver is deliberately under `reference_algorithm`, not under `attacks`, because
+Track B expects it to succeed.
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 diagnostics
+
+No row below is a model failure. Each is an API error and the harness refused to
+consume it as an attempt, as required.
+
+| Arm | Preset | Valid solved/attempts | Script-owned records | Result |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---|
+| bare | easy | 0/0 | 4 | HTTP 403 key total limit; no verdict |
+| structural hint | hard | 0/0 | 4 | HTTP 403 key total limit; no verdict |
+| placebo hint | hard | 0/0 | 4 | HTTP 403 key total limit; no verdict |
+
+Thus `hinted − placebo` is unavailable and no conclusion about hint efficacy is
+possible. The structural hint merely names the shared-residue invariant; it does
+not provide a sequence of steps. G9(c)'s measured answer and route sizes are
+1,045 characters, 262 estimated tokens, 256 atomic IDs, and 256 modular
+reductions.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_2604_24325 import make_instance, verify, DIFFICULTY
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["hard"])
+ok, reason = verify(inst, inst["answer"])
+assert (ok, reason) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+From the repository root, emit examples with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 2604.24325 20
+```
+
+After restoring OpenRouter quota, rerun the bare hardener in this result directory
+and each G9 arm in its own scratch directory; the hardener opens transcripts with
+mode `w`.
+
+## Caveats
+
+- The modulo-997 invariant makes the distribution intentionally easy to a tool or
+  to a solver that notices it. This is the Track-B compression, not a hidden
+  Track-A hardness claim.
+- `P(guess)=0/200,000` is measured under the exact stated prior—uniform partitions
+  into unlabeled blocks of four. It says nothing about arithmetic-aware guesses,
+  which are better and are why the reference and construction-aware attacks are
+  reported separately.
+- The explicit paths may contain billions of vertices; the component-length list
+  is an exact isomorphism-class representation used by the paper's own Bin Packing
+  proof. Verification checks the endpoint-concatenation witness symbolically rather
+  than materializing those vertices.
+- The reference exact-cover solver, six listed heuristics, and exact demo
+  enumeration were tried. A general ILP/SMT solver and other modulus-discovery
+  searches were not. Most importantly, the four-vendor no-tool oracle comparison
+  remains unmeasured because of the external 403 quota error.
+- `canonical_key` is complete for the relabelings represented here: a disjoint
+  union of paths is determined up to component permutation and path reversal by
+  its length multiset. The test also carries witnesses through actual source-ID
+  permutations. It does not identify different numeric instances related only by
+  scaling, because their forests are not isomorphic.
