-"""Self-contained verified generator for arXiv:2604.24325.
-
-The paper studies vertex identification into subclasses of chordal graphs.  This
-module uses its exact Identification problem on linear forests.  Both graphs are
-represented, up to isomorphism, by the edge-lengths of their path components.
-The answer partitions the source components into blocks of four; identifying
-three pairs of endpoints in each block concatenates those paths into one target
-path.
-
-Instances are inverse-generated.  The component partition is sampled first and
-the target lengths are its exact sums.  No generated instance is solved in order
-to obtain its planted witness.  Only the Python standard library is required.
-"""
